    "readme": "# Python\n\nMicrosoft's Python extension: running Python files, testing with pytest and unittest, environments and the glue for the Python tooling extensions.\n\nThis is the unmodified extension published on Open VSX, pinned to a specific version and verified to work in Diode. It ships platform-specific builds; the registry entry carries one artifact per platform.\n\n## What works in Diode\n\n**Python: Run Python File in Terminal** runs the current file in the selected environment through terminal shell integration. The **Testing** view discovers and runs pytest tests; a failed test shows its message after the line.\n\n## What does not\n\nLanguage features — completions, hover, go to definition — come from Pylance in VS Code, and Pylance is not published on Open VSX. Pair this extension with a language server from the marketplace, such as basedpyright or ruff. Debugging needs `ms-python.debugpy`, which is not in the Diode marketplace yet. Diode does not install extension packs, so install **Python Environments** (`ms-python.vscode-python-envs`) separately.\n",
